{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up","id":1370967,"title":"When did the Gauntlet go up?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-28T03:37:52-08:00","id":1370967,"title":"When did the Gauntlet go up?","content":"1000BC? 20,000BC? 1 million BC?<br /> <br /> Kindred of the East (page 8) says that in the First Age there was no Gauntlet, but as the Ages turned it went up. So was there a Wall in the Second Age? The Third? The Fourth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-28-2020, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T06:25:00-08:00","id":1371002,"title":"","content":"My guess would be third or fourth, given that the Second Age in Exalted doesn't have a Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T07:15:46-08:00","id":1371010,"title":"","content":"It can\u2019t be 1 million BC or no vampire would remember.<br /> <br /> I would say it started by the time Charon becomes the first Wraith, the gauntlet going up being the reason he was the first. As he used to live near a big river in the Occident before his death, I would put him in the old Mesopotamia.<br /> <br /> If you pick the first Pharaohs list, you have the old gods, treating them as powerful spirits, you can say there was no wall. As the Chinese empire is as old as Egyptian, you can say the origins of the Chinese empire was in the first age, so before the gauntlet goes up (good for KotE)<br /> <br /> Osisris is know for his relationship with death, his wife, Isis, was the most powerful magician of her time. If you pick those and the entire Seth x Horus thing, I would put his death as the rise of the Gauntlet as a way Isis made her husband king even after death. As a side effect, the dead and the spirits were separated too.<br /> <br /> If you pick the list of the pharaohs in Wikipedia, Osiris was pharaoh between 5180BC and 5120 BC.<br /> <br /> Osisirs was not the last god that was Pharaoh, but the Gautlet was not that strong back then, so for the next 100 years or so powerful spirits were capable of materializing. This capacity was lost eventually and the mythic empire become the first dynasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T08:02:27-08:00","id":1371017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1371002#post1371002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My guess would be third or fourth, given that the Second Age in Exalted doesn't have a Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but KotE's First Age is formless unity, it's Second Age has the Demon Kings falling, the Third Age has humans ruled by the heroic 10,000 Heroes who cast down the Demon Kings. So I think if you want to 1st ed Exalted's tenuous connection to WoD, you have to roll the ages forward by 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-28-2020, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T08:06:57-08:00","id":1371019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1371010#post1371010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can\u2019t be 1 million BC or no vampire would remember.<br /> <br /> I would say it started by the time Charon becomes the first Wraith, the gauntlet going up being the reason he was the first. As he used to live near a big river in the Occident before his death, I would put him in the old Mesopotamia.<br /> <br /> If you pick the first Pharaohs list, you have the old gods, treating them as powerful spirits, you can say there was no wall. As the Chinese empire is as old as Egyptian, you can say the origins of the Chinese empire was in the first age, so before the gauntlet goes up (good for KotE)<br /> <br /> Osisris is know for his relationship with death, his wife, Isis, was the most powerful magician of her time. If you pick those and the entire Seth x Horus thing, I would put his death as the rise of the Gauntlet as a way Isis made her husband king even after death. As a side effect, the dead and the spirits were separated too.<br /> <br /> If you pick the list of the pharaohs in Wikipedia, Osiris was pharaoh between 5180BC and 5120 BC.<br /> <br /> Osisirs was not the last god that was Pharaoh, but the Gautlet was not that strong back then, so for the next 100 years or so powerful spirits were capable of materializing. This capacity was lost eventually and the mythic empire become the first dynasty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, some interesting ideas there!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T09:32:32-08:00","id":1371031,"title":"","content":"Well, KotE core also says to become Wan Xian the soul of a mortal must cross the Wall, which means it has risen during that time. And the formation of Wan Xian means the turning of Age (Second to Third). But in First Age the spirit and material are the one, so...<br /> <br /> So I think it maybe sometime during Second Age, the most conservative estimate<br /> <br /> Fourth Age already has Wall but it\u2019s weaker. see Blood and Silk, which is set in the very last of Fourth Age, and it has some very interesting stuff<br /> <br /> You can also insult Shattered Dreams<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1371010#post1371010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the Chinese empire is as old as Egyptian, you can say the origins of the Chinese empire was in the first age, so before the gauntlet goes up (good for KotE)</div> </div> </div> </div>Emmm, in KotE the whole Chinese mortal empire was after the fall of Wan Xian, which marks the pull of wheel from Third to Fourth Age<br /> <br /> The first age is in the perfect harmony, iirc it\u2019s veil","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 02-28-2020, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T09:47:36-08:00","id":1371035,"title":"","content":"Ok. the additional info don't alter my approach (that don't count the eras, except for the reference you pointed).<br /> <br /> If we mark the Start of the mortal empire, we can point the same way I did for Egypt. The mortal empire starts in the third era, with the raise of the wall that end up forcing the spirits away from the mortal world.<br /> <br /> I may be wrong, but the fall of Wan Xian can be the same time as the end of the Egyptian mythical era (when the gods were the Pharaohs). If that's the case the entire fall of wan xian and end of the mythical egypt can be caused by the same issue (or one caused the other or vice versa). Honestly its been since I pick my KotE books or my Mummy books...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T09:54:18-08:00","id":1371037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1371035#post1371035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. the additional info don't alter my approach (that don't count the eras, except for the reference you pointed).</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole mortal empire (or, all recorded history) is the Fourth Age thing. Blood and Silk sets the Xia empire (1st Chinese empire) at the beginning of the fourth age iirc.<br /> <br /> Third Age may be much earlier than this. Shattered Dream of W20 (I don\u2019t know if it\u2019s canon) thinks the War of Shame (a War of Rage in Middle Kingdom, which was raised by corrupted Wan Xian) can date back to 12000 BC at least iirc<br /> <br /> You can look at the Blood and Silk, which is useful when finding out these question<br /> <br /> *But to be honest, it is not uncommon that two game lines contradict each other...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 02-28-2020, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T10:05:43-08:00","id":1371038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1371037#post1371037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*But to be honest, it is not uncommon that two game lines contradict each other...</div> </div> </div> </div>True in so many levels...<br /> <br /> Thats one thing they did on CoD that would be useful on WoD, they made the past a giant question mark, until they mage the book that unify all the past into a single line, including how the world was before the entire Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Thats plan ahead, and it didn't happen over the 15+ years of writing to the WoD (but come on, it was not supposed to be that big when they first start it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T10:11:22-08:00","id":1371040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1371038#post1371038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True in so many levels...<br /> <br /> Thats one thing they did on CoD that would be useful on WoD, they made the past a giant question mark, until they mage the book that unify all the past into a single line, including how the world was before the entire Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> Thats plan ahead, and it didn't happen over the 15+ years of writing to the WoD (but come on, it was not supposed to be that big when they first start it).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how oWoD works, bro. A fluff big as hell. I know your feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 02-28-2020, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T12:51:26-08:00","id":1371073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1371031#post1371031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, KotE core also says to become Wan Xian the soul of a mortal must cross the Wall, which means it has risen during that time. And the formation of Wan Xian means the turning of Age (Second to Third). But in First Age the spirit and material are the one, so...<br /> <br /> So I think it maybe sometime during Second Age, the most conservative estimate</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... Good points, thanks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fourth Age already has Wall but it\u2019s weaker. see Blood and Silk, which is set in the very last of Fourth Age, and it has some very interesting stuff </div> </div> </div>That's a Kindred of the East book? What's it about? It's not one I have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can also insult Shattered Dreams </div> </div> </div>Because it contradicts so much other stuff? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I own Shattered Dreams, and I kind of liked it, but man is it confusing when you try and mesh it with other WoD stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T13:41:09-08:00","id":1371082,"title":"","content":"This is one of those questions that, accursed idiom that it is, every ST needs to decide for the needs of their own table, chronicle, and cosmology.<br /> <br /> For me personally though, I usually use ~10,000 BCE as being around the period where history 'solidifies' and The Gauntlet rises to slowly wean pure power from the world until we can get something resembling the modern nights and our own reality.<br /> <br /> I use that era to be around the time where after millennia of a legendary pseudo-spiritual existence as kami-like (as in WtA lore, not Shinto belief) beings, the changing breeds solidified into something resembling their current form as they entered the period of internal strife and conflict with humanity caused by their newly material existence and The Gauntlet which would be the foundational reason of the Wars of Rage &amp; Impergium to follow.<br /> <br /> I also use this as around the period where Enoch was destroyed by the Deluge and The Fallen were sealed into The Pit and all the various biblical antediluvian (lower case 'A') beings were either destroyed or buried as a more 'mundane' phase of existence was born.<br /> <br /> I also use this to represent the period where the Age of Myths &amp; Legends described by Mages and The Fae end. The earliest mages fade into pre-history as the laws of magick shift towards what we recognize today and The Firstborn (Tuatha de Danaan, Fomorians, etc) begin the process of migrating into The Deep Dreaming &amp; Beyond.<br /> <br /> Again this is just all my theories and a bit of metaplot stitchery, but ~12,000-10,000 BCE is the point I use where the Multi-Resonance Layered Reality solidifies with the Material (&quot;Real World&quot;) and Umbra/Astral (Everything Else) is created beyond The Gauntlet to allow for non-mythic existence to truly begin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T14:09:26-08:00","id":1371085,"title":"","content":"Seems like everyone is going for a bit before recorded history then, rather than 100,000 years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T18:20:43-08:00","id":1371129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1371073#post1371073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a Kindred of the East book? What's it about? It's not one I have.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can treat it as a KotE book, talking about all shen (mainly Wan Gui of course) and Middle Kingdom of Dark Age (<i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,Arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000034\">more accurately, 1197AD, when is the very last of Fourth Age). A great book if you want to play games set in that time or the whole Fourth Age.</span></span></span></i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1371073#post1371073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Because it contradicts so much other stuff?</span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Emmm no I think it talks about Prehistoric a lot and may give you some points","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T18:25:35-08:00","id":1371130,"title":"","content":"Additionally I find that <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gauntlet did go up in Second Age, at least in KotE.<br /> <br /> Blood and Silk, Page 104<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> During the Second Age, the August Personage spread great Celestial Nets between the Middle Kingdom and the realms of the spirit. These nets ordered universe by separating Earth from Heaven, the real from the notional and the living from the dead. </div> </div> </div></span></b></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T21:47:21-08:00","id":1371189,"title":"","content":"The thing with oWoD though is that none of the lines make sense together at all. So its really hard to know when the Gauntlet went up. Multiple people told me this when I made the &quot;strangest aspect of oWoD&quot; thread a year ago and I've come to agree with them. The only thing you can do is go by your own personal headcanons and work from there. Because think about it:<br /> <br /> -The August Personage of Jade definitely isn't the same God the Elohim serve. Not only do they operate in different geographic regions altogether, they also run their celestial factions <b>very</b> differently, with entire different ranks and titles altogether. This isn't to mention that the Abrahamic God is probably much younger than the August Personage of Jade if we take sheer chronicality into account.<br /> <br /> -The Yama Kings never knew about the Elohim and the Elohim never knew about the Yama Kings despite supposedly serving the same entity if we are to believe August and Abraham are the same.<br /> <br /> -Elohim make no mention or even remember the Wan Xian despite supposedly being the servant &quot;creators&quot; of the universe for the Abrahamic God<br /> <br /> -Not even the Fera (Shape-Changers) even know who the hell the Elohim are and they are the oldest splat if we take into account lore chronicality. Mokole (the oldest subsplat within the Werewolf) line don't even mention the Elohim and their supposed wars on Earth. (Although this isn't really fear since D:TF was the last line for WW)<br /> <br /> Speaking of Werewolf: The Apocalypse, the whole Celestine things with Gaia, Weaver, Wryd, and Wyrm really really complicate things further for obvious reasons. Arguers saying that D:TF's &quot;multifaceted&quot; realities can lock in the entire WoD line is at best pretty weak on its self. I believe that because D:TF is directly based off the old testament of the Abrahamic religion. Now if we consider the WoD universe with all splats involved W:TA or M:TA override D:TF because like I've said before in my other thread concerning this topic- Judaism, Christianity, and Islam is pretty new compared to the other organized religions way before it. Entities that came out from the &quot;Abyss&quot; before those religions were thought (which is supposedly under Oblivion itself) couldn't possibly be bothered with a mortal religion well before their creation. The only real explanation would that Triat would be first altogether since it has influences and appearances in almost every WoD splatline after it was first introduced. It makes the most sense too. EDIT: Also realistically in the WoD universe mortal derived religions wouldn't supersede cosmic-celestine entities at all. <br /> <br /> It just seemed to me like another shoehorn from White Wolf with the whole Abrahamic motif despite coming up with unique stuff with their other lines in general anyway. Also that's even if you think the &quot;(God{s})&quot; had anything to do with the Gauntlet going up in the first place.<br /> <br /> To go back with the whole Gauntlet thing- its really not known when it came about. The only fact about the Gauntlet is that it waxes and wanes periodically. Also the Gauntlet never &quot;went&quot; up completely at all so to speak. Mage mentions &quot;splatterings&quot; where the Umbra is almost none-existent like it was in the Mythic Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 02-29-2020, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T23:23:40-08:00","id":1371197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1371189#post1371189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with oWoD though is that none of the lines make sense together at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in region the supernatural history and stuff of Middle Kingdom is a distinct thing, which is very different from the rest of the world<br /> <br /> I can recall something additionally:<br /> The \u201cCelestial Bureaucracy\u201d in KotE should refer to hierarchies of the spirit world. If you follow this then the \u201cHeaven\u201d in Middle Kingdom should be something like High Umbra Heavenly Realms, not D:tF\u2019s Heaven which makes more sense. And the servitors of August Personage of Jade should be powerful spirits just like Yama Kings, not more \u201ctraditional\u201d Elohim.<br /> <br /> Of course Demon is a very very late line, most of it can\u2019t be adopted well into older stuff. But Christian things in D:tF seem to have no place among Middle Kingdom<br /> <br /> And Wan Xian is an unique phenomenon in Middle Kingdom. In the rest of the world we can\u2019t see tracks of anything resemble them. But in the Days of Fire of D:tF, they talked about Bright Shiner (aka Hunter), which contradicts Wan Xian in many ways...<br /> <br /> When you consider something more specific, it would be more complex.<br /> <br /> In Blood and Silk, there\u2019s a Underworld Relam called Grand Library of August Personage. What\u2019s this? It says it\u2019s a true \u201clibrary\u201d of the God, but... isn\u2019t it strange?<br /> <br /> And another Umbral Realm called Realm of the First Celestial Blacksmith or something, who\u2019s this the first celestial blacksmith? A powerful spirit?<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also a level 7 Devil Tiger Rite which allow you to send a memorial to the \u201cministry of the Heaven\u201d, what\u2019s this? I recall Elohim at first because they\u2019re also called like this in Hunter and Demon (not to mention Hunter is Wan Xian\u2019s broodmate), but maybe it refers to powerful spirits like Incarna?...<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a mess. Maybe August Personage of Jade is rahter a powerful Celestine just like Gaia than true God in Demon...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 02-29-2020, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T00:27:51-08:00","id":1371202,"title":"","content":"Nope. I don't consider anything from D:TF a priority at all for the mere reason that the Elohim are based off the Old Testament (which is extremely young religion compared to many others that predated it). Since the World of Darkness is supposed to be (obviously) a mirror of our own but supernatural, D:TF makes no sense at all- not the other way around. From the WoD lens, since the Mokole are a thing that means Dinosaurs are real in WoD. That means if we go by that information, we know for a fact the Judeo-Christian trappings are mortal derived. Entities that were supposedly created by the actual Abrahamic God in the WoD universe before the creation of Earth wouldn't be a reality because before Earth was even forming (it was a giant molten lava planet) there were no Humans to think of Abrahamic religions.<br /> <br /> The WoD universe as we know it goes back as far as 10,000 BC apparently. The oldest &quot;splat&quot; mentioned within this timeframe are the Fera/Hengokai/Shape-Changers. By basic chronicality W:TA's Triat is the one that makes the most sense for the simple fact it has logical precedents and touch all aspects of the other lines too. Gaia/Wlyd/Wyrm/Weaver are all cosmic entities, not things mortals came up with in the WoD universe. They predate Earth. Since we have W:TA to start off with, that means there were all different types of Hominids (even W:TA literally mentions the Neanderthal. There were even kinfolk from them.) already on Earth. These different Hominids had high rates of endemic warfare staple of hunter-gather societies, so that unequivocally explains why both the mythologies of V:TM and D:TF are wrong because Caine obviously wasn't the first murderer, there were was no &quot;Host&quot; vs &quot;Elohim&quot; war (The Fera never mentioned it and they're the oldest known splat in the line right with the Kithain and the Awakened), and even with all this in consideration the August Personage of Jade would still predate the Abrahamic God who created these &quot;Elohim&quot; and &quot;cursed&quot; Caine.<br /> <br /> Also it makes no sense to consider August Personage of Jade just a Celestine and not just a God when it predates the Abrahamic one or even to consider both these of &quot;Gods&quot; to be more relevant than the Triat in WoD. It makes no logical sense. This why I don't like D:TF at all. It came very late in the line, tried to be the &quot;explaination&quot; for the entire WoD Universe (since it literally deals with these so called &quot;creators&quot; dispatched by 'God'), but it just made the situation worse shoehorning the Abrahamic only nonsense White Wolf moved away from. Nothing about the lore of D:TF compelled me at all after all the tidbits from the other lines.<br /> <br /> If its going to go &quot;hey we're a group of supernaturals that basically made the whole Universe and this one deity out of all the others is the right one lol XD&quot;, D:TF should've been the &quot;tie-in&quot; for WoD. Explain the Trait, explain the other supernaturals (which they didn't for the most part and only mentioned you guessed it- vampires) since they by D:TF's logic &quot;created&quot; them, explain the &quot;Age&quot; system, explain why the Elohim don't even know what the Umbra is but somehow know blather about &quot;multifaceted realities&quot;, etc. Something substantial. D:TF shouldn't be really considered relevant for lore dives because it has no connection with any of the lines at all. In my honest opinion- the Elohim are Neverborns who got disturbed by the Spirit Nukes so much they've gotten pushed out the Labyrinth and possessed human hosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 02-29-2020, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T02:31:10-08:00","id":1371212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1371130#post1371130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally I find that <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Gauntlet did go up in Second Age, at least in KotE.<br /> <br /> Blood and Silk, Page 104</span></b></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's great, thanks!<br /> <br /> Seems to fit with other stuff people have said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T03:50:32-08:00","id":1371219,"title":"","content":"Just a reminder about DtF, the Abrahamic religions were created by Lucifer after the fact as he wandered Earth.<br /> Potentially all the origin stories are accurate but just originated from different layers of reality hence why certain themes show up across multiple splats. They don't mesh perfectly together because metaphysically they're a patchwork job. DtF simply states that the Elohim served God and created reality, but that they don't know about a lot of other splats because they simply didn't come from the worldline that they created.<br /> Personally I say that the DtF was the base from which the WoD originated mostly because of VtM and DtF being compatible lore-wise with Vampire being the first line to come out and Demon being the last big line kinda makes some cool symbolism about starting with a gothic religious and ending with gothic religious as well.<br /> Basically the Gauntlet comes up as a sort of collapse point from all worldlines that causes them to sort of crumble and melt into one another. That's why the number is vague, at least to me, and the fusing worldlines still have some impact like how most of Asia is metaphysically different and distinct from other places in the world. It has a stronger presence of some of its originating worldline, resulting in slightly difference metaphysics, yet still similar enough to other worldline remains that it has a sort of convergent evolution with them. <br /> At least thats how I play it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Its quite possible that the Guantlet came up at multiple points in time, maybe in different times in different places, or everywhere in different worldline points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-29T11:02:57-08:00","id":1371996,"title":"","content":"If Lucifer and his Hosts were active on Earth since the beginning with a huge war, how come the D:TF never mention the other splats at all? How come the Elohim never mention Dinosaurs or the Mokol\u00e8 during creation of reality? Also D:TF never reconciles the supposed &quot;Epic War&quot; between Angels and Demons in regards to the other splats. If this happened for centuries, how come the Awakened, Fera, Changelings, Wraiths, and Mummies were never involved? Because the war wasn't relegated to only the traitor Elohim and loyalist Elohim- all of humanity got involved too. That means it HAS to explain why the other supernaturals were not involved ANY of the conflicts during that time period.<br /> <br /> You can <i>maybe</i> chalk it up that the other lesser Elohim had forgotten or their minds got scrambled in the so called &quot;Abyss&quot;, but Lucifer is supposedly was still active after the loss of the war- how come none of the long lived supernaturals during that era never mention or remember him?<br /> <br /> Also D:TF retcons the lore of Werewolf because it was the Weaver that uplifted humanity in the first place. How come the traitor Elohim never even mentioned the Weaver at all during the time period they were &quot;Enlightening&quot; humanity? The Triat isn't mentioned at all when it has been active since the beginning of reality in-universe wise now that I think about it. Many people who argue for the legitimacy of D:TF say that it operates in &quot;multiple realities at once&quot;, but how is that even remotely possible when this gameline deliberately didn't the even acknowledge the concept of the Umbra?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 03-03-2020, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T04:29:35-08:00","id":1372246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But to be honest, it is not uncommon that two game lines contradict each other...</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, it's not uncommon for books belonging to the SAME gameline to contradict each other. <br /> <br /> This is as intended. The mythical past it's supposed to be fuzzy to allow ST's to acomodate the cosmology as desired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T14:57:42-08:00","id":1372340,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the DTF demons being Unbourn with personality disorder.<br /> <br /> makes more sense in the entire setting than believing all the other lines being wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T15:53:36-08:00","id":1372344,"title":"","content":"Responses to some of the questions posited here as demon the fallen's advocate:<br /> <br /> \u2022Why doesn't DtF mention the other splats?<br /> -Well, they do, however they describe it through the primary paradigm of the demon's perceptions. Within the Multi-Resonance Layered Reality, I would argue the other splats all exist within the perception of the demons, as each and every splat can be simultaneously correct before the final calcification of reality.<br /> --Cain as the father of murder created violence as we understand it and revolutionized the war in horrific ways. Demons describe the greatest of G-D'a angels departing afterwards and we know from Book of Nod/Revelations of the Dark Morher those four angels cursed and then offered redemption to Caine. Later on, demons recognize the Mark of Caine on all Kindred.<br /> --The Changing Breeds are heavily implied to be the descendants of the Malhim, great and terrible warriors used by the loyalist forces as shock troops during The War. Given that we know demons are incredibly Wyrm tainted in Gaian perceptions, The Fall is almost certainly the same event on another layer of reality as The Corruption of The Wyrm.<br /> --Humans were taught the secrets of reality by the demons during The Fall, which is symbolically representing as Adam &amp; Eve eating the Fruit of Knowledge in Eden. Later on, The Watchers taught even greater secrets to humanity before the tragedy of Babel. This Age of Babel works very well as one layer of what mages describes as the Mythic Age.<br /> --Houses of the Fallen goes into great detail about how the seventh house was involved in the creation of the underworld after The Fall when humanity was cursed to know Death.<br /> --The Firstborn of the Age of Myth work perfectly well as another layer of the time of creation with the legendary war between the Tuathe de Danaan &amp; Fomorians which eventually results in Elder Dark being cast away as a mythic age comes to an end, nearly plugging into Demon's timeline.<br /> --The Ten Thousand Immortals and their corruption and becoming the Kuei-Jin is an obvious comparison but I have another which is more speculative then these others. In this, I posit that the Ten Thousand Immortals were the Nephilim on another layer of reality. Divinely imbued mortals who were created to fight a great war and were given stewardship of the world but fell to vice and corruption and had to be cast out in a great cataclysm. Sound familiar?<br /> ---A related head canon but I for one think the Wan Xian or Ten Thousand Immortals served as a first iteration of the imbued and what we know today is a deliberately weaker version so as to avoid a repeat of the previous disaster.<br /> <br /> So ultimately my first point is that Multi-Resonance Layered Reality works perfectly well for allowing every splat to be internally correct as well as cooperatively cohesive with one another.<br /> <br /> \u2022What about the Were-Dinosaurs?<br /> -This is a fair question and I would like to know more about it myself, however I do have a few responses for this.<br /> --Even within the cosmology of WtA, the idea of a prehistoric dinosaur civilization doesn't make sense within our understanding of Earth's reality. However, with the concept of Multi-Resonance Layered Reality, one can resolve this snag neatly. Yes, within one layer of reality, there were a race of sapient dinosaur people who ruled the earth yet their time of glory was destroyed in a great cataclysm. A cataclysm which was different in this layer, yet just as tied t The Fall or The Deluge as the rest. <br /> --This taken with the fact that the Technocratic Union has actively created a consensus which denies the possibility of dinosaur king's, we see how the Multi-Resonance Layered Reality remains relevant as mages maintain the capacity to alter the nature of the calcified layer that is the material reality of the WoD.<br /> --Plus, the first thing that Multi-Resonance Layered Reality was meant to explain was how a 7-Day Creation &amp; Big Bang/11+ billion years could be simultaneously accurate, so that also sidesteps the classic Dinosaurs v. Creationism debate, at least cosmologically.<br /> <br /> \u2022What Were the other splats doing?<br /> -This is where Multi-Resonance Layered Reality is once again our friend, as the other splats are happy to tell us what they were doing:<br /> --Caine was being cursed, taught by Lilith, embracing childer, and doing all the other stuff from the Book of Nod that happens before the Great Deluge. Demon even mentions Cain's role on another layer of reality in leading the militant rebels agains Abel's loyalist tribe.<br /> --The Changing Breeds tell us precisely what they were doing in early creation. Serving Gaia in peaceful harmony before the Wyrm's Corruption. Just like Angels &amp; Humanity before The Fall. After the Wyrm's Fall they begin combatting the corruption and spiritual miasma caused by the Weaver and Wyrm. Now remember that the Fallen are Wyrm (and probably weaver) tainted to an extreme and their descriptions of bestial warriors in service of a patroness called 'Gaia' seem familiar. Demons simply called them 'The Malhim'.<br /> --Ask 7 mages and get 13 answers about what was going on at the origins of everything, but from the constant descriptions of a long-lost mythic golden age in so many traditions and the eventual cataclysmic destruction of said age, we can assume that The Mythic Age of the mages are describing many varied layers of reality.<br /> --Wraiths were actively supporting the seventh house in their war against Heaven, according to the slayers.<br /> --The Firstborn Fae serve as reflections of what happened in this age in humanities perception by their very nature, but tracking their recollection to the timeline works just as nicely as the others do.<br /> --Heck, the backstory of the Kuei-Jin fits extremely well as an alternative perspective to the events of The Fall in so many ways it's honestly incredible.<br /> <br /> \u2022Thr Weaver's Gift<br /> -According to the record of the changing breeds, humanity was originally uplifted by being given gifts from The Weaver. This act rose them from their primal state and planted the seeds for the corruption to follow. You might even call this... Original Sin?<br /> --In my opinion, this example does far more to provide support for DtF's Multi-Resonance Layered Reality then it does to argue against it. Because ultimately, these four acts which I'm about to use as an example achieve the same thing as perceived in four different ways:<br /> ---Changing Breeds: Humanity is bestial but with ingenious potential. This attracts the Weaver's attention and sympathies. The Weaver longs for affection and offers humanity gifts. When they accept they are enlightened and uplifted, yet this leaves them vulnerable to spiritual corruption which the Wyrm soon exploits. Time goes on and the golden age is destroyed.<br /> ---Demon: Humanity is ignorant and beastial. Angels long to see humanity achieve its potential and be loved by them. Lucifer leads rebellious angels to grant gifts of enlightenment and love to humanity. Humanity accepts and arises to their full potential, including good and evil. This leads to God's wrath and The Fall.<br /> ---Abrahamic: Humanity is innocent within The Garden. They are persuaded to eat The Forbidden Fruit and gain the Knowledge of Good and Evil. This raises them up yet leaves them vulnerable to sin, particularly Original Sin. As punishment they are cast from Eden and cursed. Humanity must struggle forever after.<br /> ---Science: Proto-human species slowly develop and are similar to forms of primates. These proto-humans evolve and adapt and begin to resemble modern humans. At some point this evolution results in salience and understanding of abstract concepts. These new humans learn language and good and evil. This allows them to grow rapidly, yet also will become the foundation of all the tragedies and sorrows to follow.<br /> <br /> All of these four scenarios are distinct yet thematically similar, which is exactly what the Multi-Resonance Layered Reality is meant to illustrate.<br /> <br /> A paradoxical reality which allows stories to be truer then true is an excellent tool for any writer or setting to have at their disposal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 03-02-2020, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-02T19:25:48-08:00","id":1372366,"title":"","content":"The total lack of attention to and awareness of the Middle Umbra in D:tF doesn't make me very confident that you can line anything up along its schedule. It may have multiple layers in the model, but it doesn't have all of them, and that makes it very suspect. In not existing but then popping back into existence, D:tF could even be an invading reality that attempts to smooth things over after the fact, with denizens that have no place in a particular game's setting. They could exist only as the remnants of a destroyed and broken creation, turned parasitic after exiting the universe where they originated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T05:09:05-08:00","id":1372429,"title":"","content":"As always, to make sense of things one needs to emphasize certain aspects of WoD and de-empasize others.<br /> <br /> &quot;God as Gaia&quot; has the problem that most Changing Breeds don't think of Gaia as the creator of the universe. It's the Triad that creates the universe. &quot;God as Gaia&quot; starts sounding better if one mentions the theory of the &quot;Gaia that Was&quot;, that's a perception of the Triad working in harmony AS a singular Gaia entity (that's not usual Garou perception of Gaia, it's Kitsune) - and then we say that *this* Gaia it's God.<br /> <br /> The Umbra migth be explained to some extent as the different layers of reality that &quot;vanished&quot; after the War (as far as Demons know). The layers of reality are used to explain alternate facts, but they're also described as &quot;a cup of cofee being a mathematical equation and poetry&quot; (Astral Umbra cup of cofee?). One could say that, in truth, it's not that the layers don't exist anymore, but rather that they were sepparated by the Host or God and Demons just can't see them with their powers...<br /> <br /> ...only problem with this is that at least Lucifer and the Earthbound should know (if only by their interactions with splats), and they don't say a thing (except a Earthbound power that vaguely references other worlds, yet what it does looks nothing like the spiritual powers of other splats). Werewolves in the Demon ST guide don't &quot;vaninsh&quot; when they step sideways, they go to the Dark Umbra - and if Demon Werewolves don't go to the Middle Umbra, who has the rigtht to go there?. The lack of Umbra it's one of the most heavy contradictions, if you look at it carefully and with a demanding eye. <hr /><br /> I also have a certain fondness for Demon cosmology, but rather because it panders certain aspects of the cosmology of Mage that I like: M20 (and also much of the oldest material) presents the pre-history of mages saying that the first humans were gifted their powers by the Pure Ones (angels?), it's also said that the first mages (the Verbena Wyck) were the children of the Pure and humans (Nephilim?). That part of Mage Lore fits almost perfectly.<br /> <br /> The all important &quot;Consensus Shapes Reality&quot; it's covered by humans as a race having the latent potential of God - obviously they can subconsciously shape Reality. Avatars are even called god-shards by many. The fact that the Consensus doesn't reach everything can also be covered - there were and are other, pre-human, powers involved in the crafting of the universe that have/had a say.<br /> <br /> There are some edges that are harder to hammer (Like, say The One &quot;shattering&quot; into the Pure Ones doesn't fit 1/1), but I think it's easier to conciliate with Mage than, say, Werewolf (it should be no wonder, Mage and Demon are more or less anthropocentric. Werewolf isn't)<br /> <br /> ....But, of course, all of this does push the &quot;being rigth&quot; balance way too much towards the Traditions worldview (The &quot;We Are Gods In Disguise&quot; Paradigm of BoS) - and Mage won't have it. It's important for the game about &quot;figthing for reality&quot; to never show someone being fundamentally right or wrong. Hence it's a good thing that the Mage canon contradicts (or at least present options to) all that I said numerous times.<br /> <br /> Here it's where Mage and Demon clash - Demon metaplot it's way too fond of them being right about the cosmology. It never presents real doubt about Creation and their brand of monotheism - up to the point of declaring most, if not all, religions as either Earthbound or Luciferian in origin.<br /> <br /> Mage, on the other hand, cheerfully presents doubt about almost every aspect of their Lore (even the fabled &quot;Mythic Age&quot; it's more belief of the Traditions than fact - Technocrats don't attribute much wonder to the dark beginnings of the world: *this* age it's their &quot;Mythic Age&quot;). People think mages lack credibility - but in truth this uncertainty it's an important aspect of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-03-2020, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T06:07:26-08:00","id":1372437,"title":"","content":"Since a lot of this stuff is supposed to be symbolic, I'd say it happened when people started to care about the difference between recording facts and recording stories. So around the time of Herodotus. Before that, people didn't make meaningful distinctions between the stories of Amazons, and the actual reality of the people from the area Amazons supposedly came from. In other words, they didn't make a distinction between the product of their minds, and reality. Since everything about White Wolf is a big symbolism thing, that sounds like the time when the gauntlet went up: when humans made a distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T11:57:11-08:00","id":1372506,"title":"","content":"The Multi-Layered Reality theory doesn't make sense. It ignores all logic and shoehorns D:TF lore all over the place where it wouldn't make sense being at all. D:TF Elohim doesn't recognize or even acknowledge the various Umbras despite once &quot;supposedly&quot; shaping reality. Not only that it just seems like a lazy excuse for the writers at the time to throw out the other gameline lore because they were too lazy to read all the other books and consolidate. The fact is D:TF as the last splat and line to explain the actual lore of how the WoD universe came to be should've taken a waaay different route.<br /> <br /> Another reason why I believe the Elohim are just crazy Neverborn who have come to possess human bodies is because they aren't like actual WoD Demons. The real Demons in WoD know, travel, and live in all parts of the Umbra (Low Umbra not that much). Even high supreme Demon Lords like the Yama Kings have sustained domains in the Middle Umbra for millennia and they have LESSER Demonic servants. So actual Demons have been active in the WoD universe for a long time. The Baali literally have a specialized <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Daimonion\" target=\"_blank\">Discipline</a> that allow them to summon Demons. They even used utilized actual demons multiple times in the lore when they cursed the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Decani\" target=\"_blank\">Assamites</a> and not only that, Demons (not the &quot;Fallen&quot;) helped the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Baali_Wars\" target=\"_blank\">Baali assault the second city</a> by some accounts, where Caine himself supposedly had to curse the &quot;Shaitan&quot; of this bloodline. (Do note though that multiple members of this clan take up this title)<br /> <br /> How coincidental that the Spirit Nukes that the Technocrat Casey(?) Jones launched at Oblivion somehow cracked a fissure allowing these &quot;Elohim/Fallen&quot; to come out this supposed Abyss that is mentioned in D:TF lore??<br /> <br /> There is nothing in Oblivion. I'm a Wraith fan. Nothing can exist in Oblivion. The only *instance* where I heard anything surviving Oblivion is some tidbit from the Akashic Brotherhood and Jade Kingdom lore is where souls are supposed to be &quot;cycled&quot; by Oblivion then spat back out for reincarnation. Bad souls don't survive the process, just disappear from it. Other than that flaky piece of lore, nothing survives Oblivion.<br /> <br /> I believe the Spirit Nukes probably hit the Labyrinth real hard and the force simultaneously woke and spat Neverborn into the world into human bodies. The torment every Fallen has is representative of how much pain they remember when Life and Death split from eachother, forming their existence. I think this because there can't possibly be any Abyss. Nothing can exist &quot;under&quot; Oblivion because there is no site that can be active under Oblivion when there is nothing there. The whole &quot;God&quot; supposedly cursed us thing is them trying to rationalize the intrinsic painful reality of how they came into existence from that separation.<br /> <br /> Also if the Fallen were so important, how come the Wyrm and its servants don't try to make contact with them? The Wyrm has a presence everywhere in cities along with the Weaver, you'd think it wouldn't have had agent to contact these so called reality creators already? The truth is that spirits don't take entities from the Low Umbra seriously at all, where the Fallen/Neverborn came from. If the Fallen were really the bigshots, they would've been gathered up by the Wyrm or would know about the Middle and High Umbra. But they don't- which makes sense because the Neverborn have been sleeping since their creation, only subconsciously learning about things from their slumber. (which is probably why they think their &quot;Fallen&quot; having heard stories about hell and being &quot;damned&quot; from the grape-vine from what they've heard from their worshippers/minions). If your saying this splat (Elohim) are dealing with this &quot;multi-faceted reality&quot; theory, it has to make sense. But they don't even know ANY other Umbra but the Low Umbra. Literally. So I don't buy much of what D:TF is saying. They don't know the Triat, don't even know about the Astral Reaches/High Umbra, etc.<br /> <br /> Actually now that I think about it, if the Elohim are really lost Demons, why haven't the Yama Kings contacted not a single one since they've come back? You'd think they would want a family reunion. Also why is Lucifer (the supposed leader of the rebel Elohim) relegated to Earth? Why can't he side-step/materialize back into the Umbra? If that's the case he must not be as powerful as the returned Elohim are talking about at all if he can't even do that basic thing. Even worse the Yama Kings or Maejin Incarna (the Western Yama King-like entities in service of the Wrym) don't even acknowledge him at all. How do we even know this Lucifer actually exists, not something these Neverborn that came back just made up in their mental instability?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also it would explain how the Fallen have Lores. The Neverborn came into existence as soon as Life had separated from Death. This would allow them to understand how the universe works because its instinctive to them. They are entities of fundamental forces splitting. Despite being detached from life so violently, they still know how Life works from when they were still one with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 03-03-2020, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T13:20:44-08:00","id":1372523,"title":"","content":"If you prefer that scenario then go for it, it's certainly plenty interesting as an alternative and I think it has neat ideas.<br /> <br /> Personally though, I remain in favor of the Multi-Resonance Layered Reality theory of DtF. I'd say that it's actually quite internally consistent and works very well to tie together disparate elements of the WoD cosmology.<br /> <br /> I agree that Demon the Fallen had issues with its release and that the demons and their connection to the umbra deserves more investigation. I can only speculate, but I would imagine the primary reason is that demon was never revised to offer an answer to their potential umbral connections. I would also say that layered reality could work very well with the umbra if one considers that the demons were trapped just before The Delige and if that is the line of division where The Gauntlet arises. Given the nature of the umbra, I'd say that it could certainly be considered analogous to how demons described their understanding of reality, ah understanding mostly divided from the World of Darkness today by The Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> I also think it's unfair to call the authors of DtF lazy. The books have some beautiful fiction (in my opinion) and suffered from lack of revision and change of creative leadership mid-way through the process. Regardless, I refute the position that DtF doesn't address the other game lines or contradicts their lore. Superficially perhaps, but if one considers the nature of Multi-Resonance Layered Reality as described, they actually connect rather well and operate simultaneously.<br /> <br /> I agree that the demons of DtF are not the only demons in World of Darkness. Yama Kings, High Umbral Demons, Neverborn, Kupala, etc. however, I think that the existence of these multiple varieties of demons does more for the argument that DtF Fallen can exist alongside pre-existing WoD demons than it does against it. After all, we already have distinct demons coexisting fine.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not coincidental really, it's stated as one of the direct primary causes of the fallen's escape. Also, yeah, I think the Void Engineer's name was Casey Jones. <br /> <br /> Oblivion is obvious a gaping maw of destruction, we all know that. However, that same metaphysical emptiness is exactly in keeping with what the fall describe The Pit as. A prison of infinite non-existence, because Hell is the absence of G-D. Given the descriptions of what the Fallen are describing as being the location of The Pit, Oblivion makes sense.<br /> <br /> The Neverborn connection is interesting, genuinely interesting, and I think that there's something to unpack these, as either head canon, alternate canon, or an exploration.<br /> <br /> To the question of why the Wyrm hasn't reached out to The Fallen, frankly I think that agents of the Wyrm certainly would but we never had any material to explore that with. DtF came at the end of the original World of Darkness game run and because of that (and demons being the new kids on the block of material reality) we only have the vaguest brush strokes of their relationship with other splats.<br /> <br /> Again, to the thing of them only knowing if the low umbra, I'd once again suggest that this is due to them originally operating in the time before the umbra was seperate from the main material reality of WoD. The Fallen describe stories of creation that resonate with the Middle Umbra alongside quantum physics and celestial harmonies which would nicely fit the High Umbra. The demons don't talk about 'the umbra' because their frame of reference is alien and they imagine (not entirely incorrectly) that this world is fallen out of reach of its former glory.<br /> <br /> Same thing with the Yama Kings about what I said about the Wyrm earlier, although some descriptions of the Earthbound sound interesting when compared to the Yama Kings but that's just food for thought.<br /> <br /> That's a great question and who knows, maybe he does. The fate and role of Lucifer is one of the great mysteries of DtF as a setting.<br /> <br /> Well, Lucifer is a canon character so yeah, as far as canon is concerned he does exist. If 'Revelations of the Dark Mother' is to be believed, he had a direct relationship with Lilith before The Flood. Again, we also don't have any descriptions iirc of Lucifer's interactions with the Maeljin Incarna/Yama Kings because those connections weren't explored, but we have no indication that they did or didn't interact. We also can't say for certain that Lucifer couldn't access the umbra, because iirc his mechanical abilities were always left to the hands of the ST.<br /> <br /> Sure that's one way of handling lores and it's an interesting one. Or, it can be what the demons are describing, even if not exactly as they're describing. Unreliable narrators and all that.<br /> <br /> People can like or dislike DtF, that's fair enough. I even think that a lot of your ideas about the Neverborn connection of alternative are really interesting. But imo you can't just write off the actual lore for a discussion like this. Every ST can do whatever the hell they want with their friends and at their table. But if one asks a question about the setting lore as is, while discussions of alternatives are extremely interesting and I think valuable to explore, it's important to also say canon as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 03-03-2020, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T13:47:17-08:00","id":1372528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1372523#post1372523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you prefer that scenario then go for it, it's certainly plenty interesting as an alternative and I think it has neat ideas.<br /> <br /> Personally though, I remain in favor of the Multi-Resonance Layered Reality theory of DtF. I'd say that it's actually quite internally consistent and works very well to tie together disparate elements of the WoD cosmology.<br /> <br /> I agree that Demon the Fallen had issues with its release and that the demons and their connection to the umbra deserves more investigation. I can only speculate, but I would imagine the primary reason is that demon was never revised to offer an answer to their potential umbral connections. I would also say that layered reality could work very well with the umbra if one considers that the demons were trapped just before The Delige and if that is the line of division where The Gauntlet arises. Given the nature of the umbra, I'd say that it could certainly be considered analogous to how demons described their understanding of reality, ah understanding mostly divided from the World of Darkness today by The Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it leaves out a huge chunk of WoD cosmology, we cannot really call it something that works well to tie said cosmology together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also think it's unfair to call the authors of DtF lazy. The books have some beautiful fiction (in my opinion) and suffered from lack of revision and change of creative leadership mid-way through the process. Regardless, I refute the position that DtF doesn't address the other game lines or contradicts their lore. Superficially perhaps, but if one considers the nature of Multi-Resonance Layered Reality as described, they actually connect rather well and operate simultaneously. </div> </div> </div>Not mentioning the Middle Umbra, again, is a pretty good case that D:tF's conceit would need to be re-written heavily to account for more of the material from other games. Its present state might not survive the process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree that the demons of DtF are not the only demons in World of Darkness. Yama Kings, High Umbral Demons, Neverborn, Kupala, etc. however, I think that the existence of these multiple varieties of demons does more for the argument that DtF Fallen can exist alongside pre-existing WoD demons than it does against it. After all, we already have distinct demons coexisting fine.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not coincidental really, it's stated as one of the direct primary causes of the fallen's escape. Also, yeah, I think the Void Engineer's name was Casey Jones. </div> </div> </div>Xerxes Jones, IIRC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oblivion is obvious a gaping maw of destruction, we all know that. However, that same metaphysical emptiness is exactly in keeping with what the fall describe The Pit as. A prison of infinite non-existence, because Hell is the absence of G-D. Given the descriptions of what the Fallen are describing as being the location of The Pit, Oblivion makes sense.<br /> <br /> The Neverborn connection is interesting, genuinely interesting, and I think that there's something to unpack these, as either head canon, alternate canon, or an exploration.<br /> <br /> To the question of why the Wyrm hasn't reached out to The Fallen, frankly I think that agents of the Wyrm certainly would but we never had any material to explore that with. DtF came at the end of the original World of Darkness game run and because of that (and demons being the new kids on the block of material reality) we only have the vaguest brush strokes of their relationship with other splats. </div> </div> </div>Because, as noted, Demon would discount the existence of the Wyrm via the excision of everything from the Middle Umbra. That makes it difficult to maintain any kind of two-sided interpretation of anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T14:13:00-08:00","id":1372541,"title":"","content":"\u2022I agree that if it did that then it most certainly wouldn't be something that effectively tied the cosmology together.<br /> <br /> \u2022Again, referring to the umbra, while this may simply be a case of early installment weirdness, I think that a justification can be made in that simply, the umbra as we know it did not meaningfully exist as a separate concept from reality.<br /> <br /> Let me explain: the demons describe the time before as being cosmologically layeted. Reality was simultaneously a passion play, an Abraham story, and a billions of years long process of chemical and physical development. All of these existed simultaneously. Just as distinct and contradictory thoughts and concepts can exist within the umbra as part of a greater and nebulous cosmic whole.<br /> <br /> I say that the reason that demons do not refer to the umbra specifically is because they hail from a time in which the umbra was not separate from material reality as we know it today, by the gauntlet this thread began with.<br /> <br /> \u2022Ah, thank ya, Xerxes<br /> <br /> \u2022I don't think that I would say that demon's lore excise the Wyrm. They certainly don't perceive the same spirit that the changing breeds know, the same way that the changing breeds do; but that can also be said of mages or fae. The Multiple Layers of Reality allow for the Wyrm's existence to be simultaneous with that of demons.<br /> <br /> While orthodox demons may primarily think of the Wyrm as a great demon or the infamous cosmic snag perceived by Ahrimal, just because they don't perceive it through the same animist lenses as the changing breeds, doesn't mean that the Wyrm is excluded from the Multi-Resonance Layered Reality's framework.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T17:10:35-08:00","id":1372573,"title":"","content":"If the demons knew of something that would become the MU as a part of reality, they should be able to discern its separation from the other bits in the present. Its absence would probably be something that they felt keenly. Yet, nothing in the books as they were written. This is probably because the writing was trying to set up a straight take on Abrahamic fallen angels, with crossover as an afterthought; it is not unlike the other games in this regard, which are shooting for a given experience that may or may not fit into other games if you try to bolt two or more together. Hence, it has no more explanatory power than any other game's perception of others. Just as Mage's take only really applies and makes sense if you favor Mage, layered reality only applies and makes sense if you're going with Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T17:51:03-08:00","id":1372584,"title":"","content":"Mage, due to the incredible variety of paradigms, end up being the most \u201cinclusive\u201d of the splats, at least when we talk about the several parts of the umbra, the interaction with reality in general, the general politics and interaction with the other splats.<br /> <br /> Yet, it\u2019s far from an unified view (even in game they disagree with each other).<br /> <br /> Also, Mage have a very limited knowledge of the past, they know there was the mythic era, know how it may have worked but they have no real register of the workings back then. I mean, the Hermetics are probably the ones with the most detailed map of umbra (due to their maniac way to control everything), but back in the dark ages they had little in the spirits other than how they could take advantage of them in the material world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T19:04:10-08:00","id":1372602,"title":"","content":"Mage isn't the answer to grand crossover unification, either. There isn't one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T21:22:46-08:00","id":1372614,"title":"","content":"Shattered Dreams says the Gauntlet started 65 million years ago when the age of the Dragon Kings ended and the dinosaurs became extinct.<br /> <br /> I think everything exists in the same universe, but the Gauntlet isn\u2019t a Demon thing or a KotE thing. It\u2019s a Werewolf thing.<br /> <br /> I think Demon the Fallen is totally wrong when it says the Abrahamic God created the universe. I think the Triat and Gaia the Mother Goddess existed long before that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T21:49:19-08:00","id":1372618,"title":"","content":"Gauntlet just doesn't exist in W:TA. Its a common mechanic and plot device that exists in multiple splat lines. &quot;Gauntlet&quot; is just a general name for the barrier that separates the different Umbra. Also KotE of the definitely has the Gauntlet in the line, I've read it myself. Kuei-Jin call the Gauntlet the &quot;Wall&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T22:58:33-08:00","id":1372625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1372618#post1372618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gauntlet just doesn't exist in W:TA. Its a common mechanic and plot device that exists in multiple splat lines. &quot;Gauntlet&quot; is just a general name for the barrier that separates the different Umbra. Also KotE of the definitely has the Gauntlet in the line, I've read it myself. Kuei-Jin call the Gauntlet the &quot;Wall&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically, the Wall is also part of the Shroud, so it's hybridized between the Dark and Middle Umbrae. Different spirit worlds could have been cut off from the material world at different times, too; there's nothing to say that all of them happened simultaneously, especially given how the Shroud formed (human fear of death, which couldn't have existed without humans).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T04:02:42-08:00","id":1372664,"title":"","content":"FWIW, when writing for Shattered Dreams I took every gameline into account when attempting the synthesis of history.<br /> I had to prioritize W:tA for obvious reasons, but I took from all the gamelines to *some* extent. Sadly I couldn't spend the words on explicitly calling out things like the Pure Ones, but they are there. Likewise an explanation for the differing cosmologies between Europe, India, Eastern Asia, and Australia.<br /> Bearing in mind that though the book is non-canonical, it wasn't *written* to be non-canonical.<br /> <br /> The Wonderwork forever separated spirit from physical realms, but by the time of the Banestorm it was a wispy barrier that basically everyone could walk through at will. After the Banestorm it began thickening ever so slowly over time. Bear in mind Caerns/Nodes/Dragon Nests etc reduce the Gauntlet rating and there were more of those, and more powerful ones, in those times.<br /> <br /> In my first draft the Banestorm was the origin of the Gauntlet, the Dev notes said to extend it further back.<br /> <br /> One of these days I'll finish my unified synthesized WoD history and share it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T08:51:16-08:00","id":1372721,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"167\" data-vbnamecard=\"167\">nikink</a> that sounds awesome!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T17:08:47-07:00","id":1389495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1372664#post1372664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FWIW, when writing for Shattered Dreams I took every gameline into account when attempting the synthesis of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> I was just going to post that the different Changing-Breeds don't all agree with each other about when the Gauntlet formed. And the Mokole, Ananasi, and Rokea predate humanity by millions of years (so it's impossible for them to be &quot;Malhim&quot;). The Rokea don't have a story about it. But the Mokole remember the Sundering, and the Ananasi are all personally instructed by Queen Ananasi, who witnessed the event and narrates the history in Breedbook Ananasi. They tell of wars and conflicts during the Mesozoic, and the sundering of flesh from spirit in the Wonderwork 65 million years ago, when the Wyrm was first bound by the Weaver and its mind broke.<br /> <br /> Yet, most of the younger shapeshifters believe the Wall/Gauntlet, and even the fall of the Wyrm, happened later. The Shroud and the corruption of Oblivion evidently post-date the creation of humanity. So... are the younger people mistaken? Is their idea of the Wall or Gauntlet forming really their perception of a Gauntlet merely becoming too thick to cross easily? My strong preference is for the Mokole and Ananasi version of history, but I am only one person.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1372664#post1372664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly I couldn't spend the words on explicitly calling out things like the Pure Ones, but they are there. Likewise an explanation for the differing cosmologies between Europe, India, Eastern Asia, and Australia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wha... please enlighten us? Please? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1372664#post1372664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bearing in mind that though the book is non-canonical, it wasn't *written* to be non-canonical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it never published, even on Storyteller's Vault? I have the draft version, which I think is from the Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1372664#post1372664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of these days I'll finish my unified synthesized WoD history and share it.</div> </div> </div> </div>OOh! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T20:36:40-07:00","id":1389554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1389495#post1389495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wha... please enlighten us? Please? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. If it's so subtle no one has ever noticed, it's too subtle to be relevant. Much like the Caern locations - to me, each is a specific location, trackable to an accurate spot for placement on a map. For everyone else, too cryptic and generalized and thus could be almost anywhere.<br /> Ah well, my failure. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Was it never published, even on Storyteller's Vault? I have the draft version, which I think is from the Kickstarter. </div> </div> </div>No no no, I mean when we were writing the book, it was going to be canon. It was written with that assumption. It's only after it went to White Wolf for approval that it came back with the &quot;this is not canon&quot; sidebar, surprising all of us. So you have the text we wrote that got published, it's only the context that has been flipped. If we/I had known it was going to be non-canonical it would have been much easier, as I wouldn't have spent so much time, money and effort researching all the WoD histories and real world historical information that I could to synthesize something that would correlate them all (as best I could in the time and word limits available). It would have been far more fantastical.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> OOh!<br /> </div> </div> </div>: ) One day.<br /> <br /> It's proving to be quite a large project and I keep having to do real paying work to survive. But one day...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T22:59:23-07:00","id":1389576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1389554#post1389554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. If it's so subtle no one has ever noticed, it's too subtle to be relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's relevant to me.... I want to know everything. No Bastet can walk away from a secret unless it leads to Yomi Wan or Malfeas ... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1389554#post1389554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you have the text we wrote that got published, it's only the context that has been flipped. If we/I had known it was going to be non-canonical it would have been much easier, as I wouldn't have spent so much time, money and effort researching all the WoD histories and real world historical information that I could to synthesize something that would correlate them all (as best I could in the time and word limits available). It would have been far more fantastical.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if it wasn't coherent with the rest of the WoD, then it'd be harder to use it with the other books. I for one don't think all that work was wasted. I hope you don't truly feel that you wasted your efforts.<br /> <br /> Is the published text (that is for sale) much altered by the editors of Paradox/WW, or is it pretty much as it was when you and the OPP editors submitted it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-18-2020, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T11:03:20-07:00","id":1389705,"title":"","content":"You're not going to get an exact time frame, somewhere in between exalted and the events at the end of the prologue for DtF","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T11:16:01-07:00","id":1389711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1389705#post1389705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not going to get an exact time frame, somewhere in between exalted and the events at the end of the prologue for DtF</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, Exalted as part of WoD is as Non-Cannonical as Divis Mal being the Unconquered Sun, so marking Exalted in the timeline is not a good way to make a point...<br /> <br /> Same way as marking the Aberrant War as the beguining it the First Era in Exalted Timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T12:10:34-07:00","id":1389722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1389711#post1389711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I know, Exalted as part of WoD is as Non-Cannonical as Divis Mal being the Unconquered Sun, so marking Exalted in the timeline is not a good way to make a point...<br /> <br /> Same way as marking the Aberrant War as the beguining it the First Era in Exalted Timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying it because 1st ed exalted was the OWoD prehistory and it still carries a few hints of that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T20:06:06-07:00","id":1389832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1370967-when-did-the-gauntlet-go-up?p=1389576#post1389576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's relevant to me.... I want to know everything. No Bastet can walk away from a secret unless it leads to Yomi Wan or Malfeas ... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But if it wasn't coherent with the rest of the WoD, then it'd be harder to use it with the other books. I for one don't think all that work was wasted. I hop